    "body": "## Intent\nPost-merge acceptance fixture for adoption #65 / merged PR #67, following the closed pre-merge fixture #66. Add one short sentence to tests/README.md naming the two host-only EngineTests and explaining that container verification alone cannot authorize integration. Preserve existing commands and wording otherwise.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- The added sentence names both Docker engine tests and requires the separate host suite and full CI before integration.\n- Preserve all commands, tests, dependencies, workflow, policy, harness, product and architecture behavior.\n- Create the small required OpenSpec planning artifacts and one implementation PR; report actual checks and unmet gates accurately.\n- Native refinement completion starts one independent implementation worker; implementation and same-PR feedback use the declared dotnet/PostgreSQL environment. Receipts must preserve source links, evaluation outcomes and reservation release.\n\n## Scope\nDocumentation only, for the SoFa maintainer. Dependencies: #64 and #67 are merged. Accepted ADR-0006 and existing ProductShape scope remain unchanged. Security: no Docker socket inside the workload, no relaxed checks or tooling repairs. Performance and accessibility: N/A for one documentation sentence. No product or architecture decision is requested.\n\n## Operational acceptance fixture\nThe owner already authorized the bounded refinement \u2192 implementation \u2192 PR, feedback and integration-control exercise in #65. This fresh fixture verifies the post-merge native path that the earlier experiment could not prove. Do not merge this PR or claim human acceptance. The coordinating operator will give feedback, inspect integration controls with merge=false and close the test PR without merging. A green workflow is not a passed assessment; reviewRequired remains true. Preserve the candidate and report blockers if any check is unavailable or fails."
